1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,040
Second hand, and the big
one: the console store.

2
00:00:03,040 --> 00:00:05,320
It takes thirty percent of the price.

3
00:00:05,320 --> 00:00:08,740
On seventy-nine ninety-nine,
that's twenty-four dollars.

4
00:00:10,633 --> 00:00:13,013
Third hand: the card, and a twist.

5
00:00:13,013 --> 00:00:16,141
Who pays the card fee
on your eighty dollars?

6
00:00:16,141 --> 00:00:17,093
Not Rockstar.

7
00:00:18,253 --> 00:00:20,953
When you buy from a console
store, the store is the seller.

8
00:00:21,553 --> 00:00:24,653
Its name is on your receipt, and
it's the one the card system charges.

9
00:00:25,593 --> 00:00:27,993
That role has a name,
the merchant of record.

10
00:00:29,133 --> 00:00:33,105
So the card fee comes out of
the store's twenty-four dollars.

11
00:00:33,105 --> 00:00:36,629
On a typical US card, that
fee is a couple of percent,

12
00:00:36,629 --> 00:00:38,296
roughly two dollars here.

13
00:00:38,296 --> 00:00:42,590
A company Sony's size likely pays
less, but its rate isn't public.
